-- title:
--   Integrality of Laurent coefficients on the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the intersection of the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, i.e. [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$-level field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero and have Laurent expansion the image of $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$, the usual $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-invariant, under the coefficient map. Then for every element $x$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $x$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$.
--
--   This is the integrality statement for the finite chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve at level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over a discrete valuation ring: functions integral over $A[j]$ have all their $\mathsf q$-expansion coefficients in $A$. It is obtained from the existence of a Gauss-valuation subring of $K$ attached to the base change of the $q$-expansion function field, and is used in the analysis of the Drinfeld chart and the linear part of the model at the auxiliary level one prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, which allows the prime $q$ to be $2$ or $3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_exists_coeff_eq_algebraMap_of_mem_chartAlgFin_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd.lean

